# .funcignore variant used by the AGENT Function App deploy workflow.
#
# The agent Function App is deployed as `f1-fantazy-agent-func` and must
# host ONLY the `agentWebhook/` function — per the AGENTS.md isolation
# goal that "an agent rollout cannot break the Telegram bot". This file
# documents what the deploy workflow excludes from the package.
#
# How it's used: the workflow renames this file to `.funcignore` before
# zipping (in case Azure's deploy action consults it) AND explicitly
# removes the same set of paths from the working tree before handing
# the directory to `Azure/functions-action@v1` (belt-and-braces — the
# action zips the directory itself and the explicit `rm -rf` is the
# authoritative exclusion mechanism).
#
# IMPORTANT: keep this file in sync with the workflow's `rm -rf` step.

# The OTHER function — must NOT ship with the agent app.
telegramWebhook/

# Web frontend — deployed separately to Azure Static Web Apps.
web/

# Infra-as-code — not runtime artifacts.
infra/

# Dev scripts and docs — never runtime artifacts.
scripts/
docs/
.github/
.husky/
.vscode/
AGENTS.md
readme.md

# Test + tooling files.
coverage/
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.ts
jest.config.js
eslint.config.mjs
.eslintignore
.prettierrc
.gitignore
.funcignore.agent

# Secrets and local-only config.
local.settings.json
.env
.env.*

# Source-map / TS leftovers (mirrors the default .funcignore).
*.js.map
*.ts
.git*
